From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikita Maslo <nikitamalco203@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 May 2025 16:22:00 +0300
Subject: mmc: sd: ignore sd_read_ext_regs() failure during card init

Some SD cards found in the field advertise SD spec >= 7.00 but then fail
or time out when the extension registers are read back. mmc_sd_init_card()
treats that as fatal and aborts, so the card never enumerates and the board
does not boot from it at all.

Downgrade the failure to a no-op: the extension registers only carry
optional features (power management, performance enhancement, cache), so
ignoring a read error simply leaves those features unused instead of
throwing the card away.

Carried by Armbian for the NAPI-C / NAPI2 boards, which ship with such
cards; it is harmless on well-behaved cards, where sd_read_ext_regs()
succeeds anyway.

Signed-off-by: Nikita Maslo <nikitamalco203@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/mmc/core/sd.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/core/sd.c b/drivers/mmc/core/sd.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/core/sd.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/core/sd.c
@@ -1538,8 +1538,8 @@ static int mmc_sd_init_card(struct mmc_host *host, u32 ocr,
 	if (!oldcard) {
 		/* Read/parse the extension registers. */
 		err = sd_read_ext_regs(card);
-		if (err)
-			goto free_card;
+		//if (err)
+		//	goto free_card;
 	}
 
 	/* Enable internal SD cache if supported. */
-- 
Armbian

